  "answer_text": "**wakehealth.edu** is the official website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist** (formerly known as Wake Forest Baptist Health), a nationally recognized academic medical center and healthcare system based in Winston-Salem, North Carolina. \n\nIt serves as the academic and research core for the **Wake Forest University School of Medicine** and is part of **Advocate Health**, one of the largest non-profit health systems in the United States.\n\nHere is an overview of what you can do on the website and how the system operates:\n\n### 1. Patient Portal (MyAtriumHealth)\n* **The Transition:** The system's former patient portal, *myWakeHealth*, was fully transitioned to **MyAtriumHealth**. \n* **How to Log In:** If you were a previous user of myWakeHealth, you can use your existing username and password to log into the MyAtriumHealth portal. \n* **Features:** Through the portal (available online or via the MyAtriumHealth app), patients can:\n  * Message their care teams\n  * Schedule, reschedule, or view upcoming appointments\n  * Access lab and test results\n  * Request prescription refills\n  * View doctor notes and medical history\n  * Pay medical bills\n\n### 2. Clinical & Medical Services\nThe website allows users to find care across North Carolina and parts of the surrounding region, including:\n* **Find a Doctor:** Search for primary care doctors and specialists by name, specialty, or location.\n* **Locations:** Find information on the flagship **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center** in Winston-Salem, Brenner Children\u2019s Hospital, regional hospitals, and urgent care clinics.\n* **Specialties:** Access information on world-class programs in cancer care (Comprehensive Cancer Center), heart and vascular care, orthopedics, neurosciences, and pediatric care.\n\n### 3. Education and Research\nBecause of its academic integration, `wakehealth.edu` also serves as a portal for:\n* **Wake Forest University School of Medicine:** Information on MD programs, residency and fellowship training, nursing, and physician assistant (PA) programs.\n* **Clinical Trials:** Resources for patients interested in participating in medical research studies and trials.\n\n*If you are trying to access your patient medical records or book an appointment, you can head directly to [wakehealth.edu](https://www.wakehealth.edu) and select the **MyAtriumHealth** or **Find a Doctor** links at the top of the homepage.*",
